olset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UNpuWYkTPq6BD2jrkso6SV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked and both reservations are confirmed. There was a problem during booking, but nothing was booked twice.\n\n**What's booked:**\n- **Flight R0001:** F100, SFO \u2192 JFK nonstop on 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. The one-stop flight at $199 was cheaper but had a stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel R0002:** Midtown Lodge (H1), New York, 2 nights checking in 2026-11-12, $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under $1000, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What went wrong:** I tried to book both together with book_trip, but it timed out. When I retried, the service reported that the original request had only partly worked: the flight was booked, but an internal error stopped the hotel booking. I checked Dana's reservations to confirm only the flight existed, then booked the hotel on its own. That's why there are two separate reservations instead of one combined trip.", "type": "text"}]}]}